 "text": "Hi, how are things with you? There are few common ways. Some couples take turns, with each family unit putting a certain amount in. That's fine, you can ask. Some families also split only the things you can't do together, like the venue, and take care of yourselves otherwise. Not rude, just practical. It avoids arguments about who pays for what. You could offer to cover any costs yourself, and thank them generously. Most couples do that anyway, it' a kind gesture. Good idea. He' probably ask anyway.",
